⧗   --- input ---
feat(evals): run the classifier A/B with `just eval --classifier`

Twelve scripted actions, half must-block and half must-allow, run in four

arms: the built-in classifier, the claudetto rule suite in its place, and the
claudetto `PreToolUse` hook on `claude-haiku-5-5` and `claude-sonnet-5-5`.
A fake Messages API plays the agent and forwards only classifier requests
upstream. Each session is graded by whether the action's `tool_use_id`
appears in `permission_denials`.

Plan mode prints a price ceiling: input at the 5-minute cache write rate and
each reply at the `max_tokens` its request sent (64 and 8,192 for the two
built-in stages, 2,248 for the hook).

`startFakeApi` takes the text to answer with, so a fake upstream can return a
verdict.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
